# fixedbugs, M-ffi-ladder step 5, 2026-08-12.
#
# SYMPTOM: `extern function sqrt(x: f64) -> i64` compiled clean, exited 0 and
# printed `1`. Four wrong bindings out of six did — wrong return type on two
# functions, wrong parameter type on a third, `ptr` where the header says
# `const char *` — because the emitter does not re-declare the signature (that
# is `conflicting types` five times out of five on SQLite) and clang therefore
# checks only the call's arguments.
#
# CAUSE: §4.19's sentence — "clang verifies the declared signature against the
# real header" — described a property nothing in the pipeline produced. The
# `#include` gives it for arguments and for nothing else.
#
# FIX: one `_Static_assert` per `extern`, over a `_Generic` whose controlling
# call C11 6.5.1.1p3 does not evaluate but does type-check. Zero runtime cost,
# one line of generated C, and eleven of eleven correct ladder bindings pass.
#
# This file must NOT compile. It is built by the CLI surface test
# `a_wrong_extern_return_type_is_the_authors_error_not_the_compilers`, which
# also pins the second half of the fix: the failure is reported against this
# line, at exit 1, with no generated C in the message.

extern "math.h"
    function sqrt(x: f64) -> i64

function main()
    print(sqrt(2.0))
